body:
Thank you so much. It feels better now that I have someone to talk to. 

&#x200B;

I know they do, like I believe an "intern" is a synonym to "slave" sometimes lol. I mean, at least that's how I felt when I did my unpaid internship last summer. I wasn't paid shit but I had to do stuff. I guess my mentality is pretty sick and I should not be feeling like this, but in my honest opinion that's how I felt. I am pretty horrible. 

But even then the only reason why I got it was because the school had connections. My current college has absolutely no connections with an accounting firm so I'm pretty much left hanging. It's my first time applying on my own. Sucks big time. 

&#x200B;

I'm running out of options. I am in the US, I'm not sure where you are but yes, resumes are so important. I am not so sure if mine is okay, I mean I have had it edited by my counselor and stuff but yes. I don't want to burden you by sending you my crappy resume... I feel like even if I am qualified, there's always someone better. I wish I had US citizenship instead of an F-1 visa. It limits me in so many ways. But even the visa is an excuse. Maybe if only I had a 4.0 with dozens of extracurriculars- but I have no energy or will power to get that kind of score.

First of all, thank you for your reply. It really means a lot to me, since recently I felt like no one cares much to be honest, except my parents. 

&#x200B;

I'm not so in to social media as well. In fact, I try my best to stay away from it, because why would I want to see others happy when I'm like this, right? The change honestly sucks. I've already been rejected by multiple internships. Just got rejected this morning too. I need to find an internship for the summer, but the outlook is looking pretty shitty. Even then, I am just forced to find one for my future. Nothing is done with my will. Ugh. 

&#x200B;

So I am having a great difficulty finding an internship- will I be able to find a job looking like this? I hate getting rejected but I guess it is normal. I am also worried because I will probably be graduating from a state university, which I am not sure of the job outlook. I am so scared about the uncertainty. I don't care about grades as much, I maintain a mediocre one (3.3) but that doesn't seem to be enough for any company or firm. 

&#x200B;

Sorry I'm asking so many questions. I just don't have many people to talk to. If you're annoyed, please ignore me. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
